{"name":"Jackal","hex":"#a9a093","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jackal","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of certain wild canids of the genera Lupulella and Canis, native to the tropical Old World and smaller than a wolf.","A person who performs menial or routine tasks; a dogsbody."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To perform menial or routine tasks"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jackal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jackal","blocks":[{"text":"Jackals are canids native to Africa and Eurasia. While the word jackal has historically been used for many canines of the subtribe canina, in modern use it most commonly refers to three species: the closely related black-backed jackal and side-striped jackal of Central and Southern Africa, and the golden jackal of south-central Europe and Asia. The African golden wolf was also formerly considered a jackal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Flickr_-_Rainbirder_-_Golden_Jackal_%281%29.jpg/330px-Flickr_-_Rainbirder_-_Golden_Jackal_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jackal","wikidata":"Q125525"},{"title":"Jackal (Marvel Comics character)","blocks":[{"text":"The Jackal is an alias used by two supervillains appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics, usually depicted as enemies of the superhero Spider-Man. The original and best known version, Miles Warren, was introduced in The Amazing Spider-Man #31 as a professor at the fictional Empire State University. Later storylines established him as also being a scientist researching genetics and biochemistry, and revealed an unhealthy romantic obsession he had developed for Gwen Stacy. Driven mad with jealousy and grief after Gwen's death, he creates the Jackal alter ego to seek revenge on Spider-Man, whom he holds responsible. To this end, he trains himself in martial arts and builds a green suit and gauntlets with claw-like razors. Although the Jackal initially did not possess any superpowers, he later gained enhanced strength, speed, and agility by mixing his genes with those of an actual jackal."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/85/Jackal_%28Marvel_Comics_-1975%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jackal_(Marvel_Comics_character)","wikidata":"Q2584005"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Jackals.png/500px-Jackals.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Jackals.png/500px-Jackals.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJackals.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/L._m._mesomelas%2C_Sunday%27s_River_Valley_Local_Municipality_3.jpg/500px-L._m._mesomelas%2C_Sunday%27s_River_Valley_Local_Municipality_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/L._m._mesomelas%2C_Sunday%27s_River_Valley_Local_Municipality_3.jpg/1280px-L._m._mesomelas%2C_Sunday%27s_River_Valley_Local_Municipality_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/L._m._mesomelas%2C_Sunday%27s_River_Valley_Local_Municipality_3.jpg/500px-L._m._mesomelas%2C_Sunday%27s_River_Valley_Local_Municipality_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AL._m._mesomelas%2C_Sunday's_River_Valley_Local_Municipality_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/CANIS_ADUSTUS_dans_le_park_zoologique_de_kinshasa_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-CANIS_ADUSTUS_da